{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/625601-azer-s-custom-devotions","id":625601,"title":"Azer's Custom Devotions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-13T09:28:44-07:00","id":625601,"title":"Azer's Custom Devotions.","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Wolf in Sheep\u2019s Clothing</span></span></b></b></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">[ Obfuscate 1, Resilience 1 ]</span></span></b><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Some times for Elder Nomads, Travelling can be dangerous endeavour, so some kindred are masters the art of hiding himself to such a degree that he may subvert some of the stains that undeath leaves upon his soul. This Devotion takes that to another level: The character's Beast becomes like a trapdoor, or a wolf in sheep's clothing, Concealing itself as to fit in with with Kindred of lower potency. This Devotion costs 1 XP.</span></span></i><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> --</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dice Pool:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">This power involves no roll, and is considered &quot;always on.&quot; </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Effect: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The character can make their blood potency appear lower, up-to their dots in Obfuscate, Down to zero, where they do not trigger the Predator's Taint. Therefore, if lowered to Blood Potency Zero, the character doesn't even appear as a vampire to other Kindred who see him. Kindred who can discern auras fail to register the vampire as undead; his aura is no different from a mortal's (the colors are not pale like a normal Kindred's). Note that this power doesn't render the user immune to the Predator's Taint himself, he merely doesn't cause the reaction in others. The character may turn off this power if he wishes, Note also that uses of Auspex may call this power into question, Triggering Clash of Wills.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5519-azerkatil","user":"Azerkatil","date":". 08-13-2015, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5519-azerkatil","name":"Azerkatil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T11:56:03-07:00","id":625715,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate 1 alone already hides your predatory aura as nonexistent. And predatory auras don't register blood potency as a numerical value. Just whether or not someone is a vampire trying to intimidate, seduce, or one-up you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:51:25-07:00","id":625760,"title":"","content":"I would say that it looks like a first edition devotion, but then it's nearly identical to Obfuscate 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T14:51:35-07:00","id":625953,"title":"","content":"Not a bad idea, but currently moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}